THOUGHT: The field `layer` is annotated `@Nullable`, so NullAway flags `this.layer.createGraphics()`. In the constructor, `layer` is always assigned from `Imaging.getCompatibleImage`, which likely returns non-null, but the annotation forces us to treat it as nullable. The safest minimal fix is to add a null check in `updateSection` and return early if `layer` is null, similar to the color check. Then I must run the build to confirm the NullAway error count decreases by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/litiengine && sed -i '55,72s/^  public void updateSection(Rectangle2D section) {
    if (this.getColor() == null) {
      return;
    }

    int minX = (int) Math.floor(section.getX());
    int minY = (int) Math.floor(section.getY());
    int maxX = (int) Math.ceil(section.getMaxX());
    int maxY = (int) Math.ceil(section.getMaxY());
    Rectangle aligned = new Rectangle(minX, minY, maxX - minX, maxY - minY);

    final Graphics2D g = this.layer.createGraphics();
    this.clearSection(g, aligned);
    g.setClip(aligned.x, aligned.y, aligned.width, aligned.height);
    g.translate(aligned.x, aligned.y);
    this.renderSection(g, aligned);
    g.dispose();
  }/  public void updateSection(Rectangle2D section) {
    if (this.getColor() == null || this.layer == null) {
      return;
    }

    int minX = (int) Math.floor(section.getX());
    int minY = (int) Math.floor(section.getY());
    int maxX = (int) Math.ceil(section.getMaxX());
    int maxY = (int) Math.ceil(section.getMaxY());
    Rectangle aligned = new Rectangle(minX, minY, maxX - minX, maxY - minY);

    final Graphics2D g = this.layer.createGraphics();
    this.clearSection(g, aligned);
    g.setClip(aligned.x, aligned.y, aligned.width, aligned.height);
    g.translate(aligned.x, aligned.y);
    this.renderSection(g, aligned);
    g.dispose();
  }/' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/graphics/ColorLayer.java && ./gradlew compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -i "NullAway" -n new_build_output.log | tail -n 5```

